{
  "about": "Slice 2c.12a (issue #198). The variables a workflow might set, in the job's env, the step's env or a GITHUB_ENV write, to change what the egress action's own steps do with the key they hold. tests/egress/runner-variables.py reads this file; the escape tests' runner-variables jobs set every name in 'names' each of the three ways and record what a step run as the action's own steps are (/usr/bin/python3 -I -S, plain and inside a composite action) sees. A workflow's env keys are case-insensitive (with HTTPS_PROXY beside https_proxy in one env, actionlint refused the file and GitHub did not run the workflow: runs 43933659829 and 43933634402), so the lower-case names in 'case_twins' are set only through GITHUB_ENV; through the other two channels they are recorded as their upper-case twin left them. 'expected' is what GitHub-hosted ubuntu-24.04 showed; a difference fails the job. Values are made-up paths and words, never secrets.",
  "measured": "GitHub-hosted ubuntu-24.04, escape tests run 43934052838 (2026-11-16), on 1f29a30; first required in run 43935054655, on 01274ec",
